-- title:
--   Degree-one places extend to a constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $K'$ be fields equipped with $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structures, let $\sigma : K \to K'$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$. For a field $L$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ write `laurentBaseChange L F₀` for the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$ under `coeffEmb L` $=$ `coeffMap (algebraMap ℚ L)`. A `Place` of a field $F$ over $L$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $\operatorname{im}(L \to F)$, not equal to all of $F$, and a principal ideal ring; its degree is the $L$-dimension of its residue field, and $\operatorname{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of the associated height-one-spectrum valuation, an integer-valued order function. Let $v$ be such a place of `laurentBaseChange K F₀` over $K$ with $\deg v = 1$. Then there exists a place $w$ of `laurentBaseChange K' F₀` over $K'$ with the following two properties. First, whenever $x$ lies in `laurentBaseChange K F₀` and $x'$ in `laurentBaseChange K' F₀` have $x' =$ `coeffMap σ` $x$ as Laurent series, $w.\operatorname{ord} x' = v.\operatorname{ord} x$. Second, for every type $\iota$, every nonempty finite subset $s$ of $\iota$, every family $c : \iota \to K'$ and every family $x$ of elements of `laurentBaseChange K F₀` such that the $c_i$ are independent over $K$ through $\sigma$ in the sense that any $a : \iota \to K$ with $\sum_{i \in s} \sigma(a_i) c_i = 0$ has $a_i = 0$ for all $i \in s$, and such that $x_i \neq 0$ for all $i \in s$, any $y$ in `laurentBaseChange K' F₀` whose underlying Laurent series is $\sum_{i \in s} c_i \cdot$ `coeffMap σ` $x_i$ satisfies $w.\operatorname{ord} y = \min_{i \in s} v.\operatorname{ord} x_i$. Neither uniqueness of $w$ nor $\deg w = 1$ is asserted, and $\sigma$ is not assumed injective.
--
--   This is the classical fact that a place of degree one of a function field extends to a constant field extension with ramification index one, here in the concrete form of fields of Laurent series generated by a fixed subfield $F_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, together with the computation of the extended order of a combination of elements with constants independent over the base. It is used in the estimates for hyperplane sections on the modular curve, in particular by [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_defect_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_defect_le), [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_sum_log_secVal_ge`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_sum_log_secVal_ge) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_log_secVal_sub_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_log_secVal_sub_le), the intended instance being $F_0$ a field of modular functions with $K$ the algebraic numbers and $K'$ the complex numbers.
